SUMMARY:Latent Factor Point Processes for Patient Representation in Electro
 nic Health Records
LOCATION:French Family Science Center 4233\, Durham
DESCRIPTION:Parker's research aims to develop statistical methods to tackle
  the unique challenges presented by multi-institutional biomedical data co
 llection initiatives. In particular\, he is focused on understanding how t
 o best analyze large-scale electronic health records data drawn from diver
 se populations spread across heterogeneous healthcare systems. This work r
 elies on methodological ideas from nonparametric and high-dimensional stat
 istics\, optimization\, and time series modeling. | Source: Duke Universit
 y Events (university-wide\, all categories) | Cost: unknown
URL:https://calendar.duke.edu/
