SUMMARY:‘Never A Bad Peace: Celebrating 250 Years of American Diplomacy
  with Adam Howard
LOCATION:FedEx Global Education Center\, Nelson Mandela Auditorium\, Chapel
  Hill
DESCRIPTION:In 1783\, Benjamin Franklin wrote\, “May we never see another
  War! for in my Opinion there never was a good War\, or a bad Peace.”\
 n\n \n\nIn this Diplomatic Discussion\, the keynote lecture of Diplomacy W
 eek 2026\, Adam Howard\, former chief historian at the U.S. Department of 
 State\, discusses three pivotal moments in American history shaped by the 
 work of talented diplomats: the Revolutionary War\, the Civil War and the 
 aftermath of World War II.\n\n \n\nVice Provost for Global Affairs and Chi
 ef Global Offic | Source: UNC Chapel Hill Events Calendar (university-wide
 ) | Cost: unknown
URL:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/never-a-bad-peace-celebrating-250-years-
 of-american-diplomacy-with-adam-howard
